      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fairview Park began as part of Rockport Township, later becoming the Rocky River hamlet before carving out its own identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairview_Park%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village incorporated in 1903, split in 1910, with the north becoming Rocky River and the south taking the name Goldwood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairview_Park%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1947 opening of Fairview Shopping Center on Lorain Road drew former Cleveland residents and sparked post‑war growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
